msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"New month, new Quarkus feature release, you know the drill:\n"
"Quarkus 2.10.0.Final has landed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This version is a mix of exploratory work and refinements on existing "
"extensions:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Preliminary work on Loom's virtual threads"
msgstr ""

msgid "GraphQL non-blocking support"
msgstr ""

msgid "Kubernetes service binding support for Reactive SQL Clients"
msgstr ""

msgid "`CacheKeyGenerator` for cache extension"
msgstr ""

msgid "And much more!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 2.9, please refer to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"wiki/Migration-Guide-2.10[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Preliminary work on Loom&#8217;s virtual threads"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Quarkus team started experimenting with Loom's virtual threads and https:"
"//github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/24942[a first pull request] was merged."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is still very rough and the API will be subject to change  but if you are "
"interested in Loom's virtual threads, feel free to give it a try."
msgstr ""

msgid "Expect more development and announcements in the coming months."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To learn more about this effort, check out https://developers.redhat.com/"
"devnation/tech-talks/integrate-loom-quarkus[the video of Clément's and "
"Arthur's talk]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus offers both imperative and reactive programmatic paradigms\n"
"and we work hard making sure both are exposed across the board."
msgstr ""

msgid "The GraphQL extensions now support non-blocking workloads."
msgstr ""

msgid "SmallRye Reactive Messaging upgrade"
msgstr ""

msgid "SmallRye Reactive Messaging has been upgraded to 3.16.0."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We added Kubernetes service binding support for the Reactive SQL Clients "
"extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid "CacheKeyGenerator for cache extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus-cache` extension was automatically generating cache keys from "
"method parameters without a way to customize them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A new contract `CacheKeyGenerator` was introduced in 2.10 to allow for this "
"customization."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"quarkus-bootstrap-maven-plugin deprecated in favor of quarkus-extension-"
"maven-plugin"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus-bootstrap-maven-plugin` has been deprecated in favor of the "
"`quarkus-extension-maven-plugin`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This only has impact on extension developers who should switch to the new "
"plugin."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We will keep publishing the deprecated plugin for a while so you it is not "
"urgent to switch to the new one."
msgstr ""

msgid "Better infrastructure for JDBC driver extensions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A contributor started working on a JDBC driver extension for SQLite and we "
"improved the infrastructure for external JDBC driver extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most notably, it is now possible to indicate which Hibernate ORM dialect "
"should be used by default even for external JDBC driver extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quiltflower decompiler support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When writing Quarkus extensions, it is often useful to decompile the "
"generated source code\n"
"to better understand what's going on."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We used Fernflower for that until now but we have switched to Quiltflower "
"which provides a better output."
msgstr ""

msgid "New guides"
msgstr ""

msgid "We added several new guides:"
msgstr ""

msgid "link:/guides/stork-kubernetes[Using Stork with Kubernetes]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"link:/guides/security-openid-connect-client-reference[OpenId Connect Client "
"Reference Guide]"
msgstr ""

msgid "link:/guides/podman[Using Podman with Quarkus]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/2.10.0.CR1[2.10.0.CR1] and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/2.10.0.Final[2.10.0.Final] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

